<title>MALAYSIA: Malaysia to collect rubber cess from consumers.</title>
<headline>Malaysia to collect rubber cess from consumers.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Malaysia will collect a rubber cess, used for replanting and research, from consumers instead of producers, Primary Industries Minister Lim Keng Yaik said on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;From January 1, 1998, we will collect the cess ex-factory, instead of ex-farm,&quot; Lim told a news conference.</p>
<p>He said the move was to recover nearly 40 million ringgit which the government has been losing out yearly in uncollected cess, or tax.</p>
<p>Rubber consumers have not been paying the 13.77 cents per kg of rubber they bought from local producers.</p>
</text>
